# Senior React Native — Checklist & roadmap (30-day JD-driven)

This document complements `project-context.mdc`: build **Senior Mobile App Engineer (React Native)** solidly enough to interview at **many company types** (product, agency, enterprise, startup—not locked to one vertical), combining **project-first** work with **official docs** in **Section 7** (30 days).

---

## 0. "Start day N" — what the AI reads & does (shared context)

When you say **"Start day 1"**, **"Start day 2"**, … **"Start day 30"** (or variants like _"Today is day 1"_, _"Do day 3"_), AI **has context and can execute** without repeating the whole roadmap. **`project-context.mdc` — Strict mode:** right/wrong is explicit; if wrong, fix—and **do not** advance the day if DoD is not met.

### Trigger phrases

| You say | Meaning |
| --- | --- |
| `Start day 1` … `Start day 30` | Start exactly **one day** in the Section 7 schedule (docs + project + review) |
| `Today is day N` / `Do day N` | Same as "Start day N" |

### Context order the AI should read (priority)

1. **`project-context.mdc`** — Senior goal, **Strict mode**, background, what you don't want, mentor role.
2. **`day-playbooks.mdc` (this file)** — Section **0** + **1** (knowledge frame) + **2–3** + **7** for **Day N** (docs + project + review).
3. **`day-NN.mdc`** (if present in the same folder) — Detailed playbook: steps, docs, exercises, review questions, interview prompts, DoD.

### Expected AI behavior

- **Hands-off:** **do not** run `create-expo-app`, `npm`, `git`, etc. for you—**unless** you explicitly ask. Give **steps** and **sample commands** for **you** to run locally.
- On **"Start day N"**: if **`day-NN.mdc` is missing** → **create** `day-NN.mdc` (guide + DoD + review questions), then follow it; if it **exists** → open and follow.
- Second source is always **`day-playbooks.mdc` Section 7** (**Day N** row).
- **Always** state prerequisites: e.g. Day 5 needs auth context from Day 4; if missing, say to do Day 4 first.
- Edit **files in the repo** (code, config) only when you ask for a specific fix—**do not** create a new project for you unless you ask.
- For each day: give a **doc link** (per Section 7), **build task** matching Section 7, then **review + interview** questions.
- **Strict mode:** grade review answers and DoD **by criteria**, no hand-waving; wrong technical takes get **pushed back** and corrected.

