### 7.1 30-day table

**Review** column: **write short answers** (or speak) after you commit that day's work; paste to AI to grade.

| Day | Read (official doc — 15–30 min) | Build (Expo project — 60–90 min) | Review (drill questions) |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| **1** ✅ | — (done) | `create-expo-app` (TS), `src/features`, `src/shared`, `src/app`, README goals, placeholder screen. | Why feature folders vs dumping `screens/`? What is a feature `index.ts` public API for? |
| **2** ✅ | — (done) | ESLint + Prettier + path alias `@/`; `strict: true`; commit convention. | What does `strict: true` do for a large team? When is `any` temporarily OK? |
| **3** ✅ | — (done) | Light theme + `AppText`/`Button` in `shared/`; typed props. | When to split `shared/` vs keep in feature? |
| **4** | TS Handbook — **Generics** (`typescriptlang.org/docs/handbook/2/generics`). | `api/` layer: typed `ApiResponse<T>`, `Result<T, E>` union, axios/fetch wrapper, single error-handling interceptor. | How do API response types differ from domain/UI types? Write a `Result<T, E>` — when union vs generic? |
| **5** | Expo SecureStore docs + React Navigation — **Authentication flows** (`reactnavigation.org/docs/auth-flow`). | Fake login form + mock JWT storage with `SecureStore`; protected navigation (auth stack vs app stack); mock 401 → logout. | Describe auth state machine (4 states). Why `AsyncStorage` isn't enough for refresh tokens? |
| **6** | TS Handbook — **Utility types** + **Mapped types** + **Discriminated unions** (`typescriptlang.org/docs/handbook/2/types-from-types`). | Refactor existing types: discriminated union for API error states; `Readonly<>`, `Pick<>`, `Partial<>` on domain models; branded type for `UserId`. | When is a discriminated union better than `isError: boolean`? Give one example from the repo. |
| **7** | ADR format — read `adr.github.io` (5 min) + React Navigation — **Nesting navigators** docs. | Draft `docs/ADR-001-feature-structure.md` (problem → options → decision → consequences); draft `ARCHITECTURE.md` (data flow, auth, errors in one diagram or table). | Explain the app architecture to a non-technical PM in 2 minutes. |
| **8** | TanStack Query — **Important defaults** + **Query invalidation** + **Optimistic updates** (`tanstack.com/query/latest/docs/framework/react/guides`). | Replace or augment existing fetch with TanStack Query: `staleTime`, `gcTime`, `invalidateQueries` after mutation, one optimistic update on a list item. | When does `stale-while-revalidate` help on mobile? When does it hurt? When should you use Redux alongside TanStack Query? |
| **9** | Supabase Realtime docs — **Broadcast / Postgres Changes** (`supabase.com/docs/guides/realtime`) OR WebSocket MDN basics. | Add real-time data: subscribe to a channel (Supabase) or open a WebSocket; update list in UI on new event; add polling fallback (`refetchInterval`) for environments without WS. | WebSocket vs polling vs SSE — when would you choose each on mobile? |
| **10** | Expo Notifications docs — **Push tokens + handlers** (`docs.expo.dev/push-notifications`). | Register for push token; handle foreground notification (show in-app banner); handle background tap (navigate to detail); stub server-send with Expo Push API tester. | Push vs in-app messaging? What happens to a push handler when the app is killed? |
| **11** | Expo `AppState` docs + `expo-background-fetch` overview (`docs.expo.dev/versions/latest/sdk/app-state`). | Listen to `AppState` changes (active/background/inactive); cancel or pause network requests on background; show "reconnecting" banner on foreground return. | What happens to in-flight network requests when app moves to background? How do you handle race conditions on foreground return? |
| **12** | TanStack Query — **Persistence** (`tanstack.com/query/latest/docs/framework/react/plugins/persistQueryClient`) + `@react-native-async-storage/async-storage` docs. | Persist query cache with `AsyncStorage`; add offline detection banner (`NetInfo`); show stale data with a "last updated" label when offline. | What is `stale-while-revalidate`? What are the risks of showing stale data without a clear indicator? |
| **13** | React docs — **Context** (`react.dev/learn/passing-data-deeply-with-context`) + read about multi-tenant SaaS patterns (any short blog/article). | Add `TenantProvider` context: tenant ID + user role; make API calls include `X-Tenant-ID` header via interceptor; render different UI sections based on role (admin vs viewer). | How is multi-tenant auth different from single-tenant? Where do you put the role check — component, hook, or route guard? |
| **14** | — (review day — no new doc). | Draw a data-flow diagram (even in ASCII or a Markdown table) showing: user action → hook → query/mutation → API → state update → re-render. Commit to `docs/data-flow.md`. | Write answers to: (1) When Redux vs TanStack Query? (2) How does your offline strategy handle conflicting writes? (3) What is an optimistic update and when does it fail? |
| **15** | Reanimated docs — **Worklets + shared values + useAnimatedStyle** (`docs.swmansion.com/react-native-reanimated/docs/fundamentals`). | Add one animated component: fade-in on mount (`withTiming`), slide-in on list item appear (`withSpring`); use `useSharedValue` + `useAnimatedStyle` — no `Animated` API. | Reanimated `useSharedValue` vs React `useState` — what is the key difference? When would you still use `Animated` from RN core? |
| **16** | Gesture Handler docs — **Tap + Pan gesture** (`docs.swmansion.com/react-native-gesture-handler/docs`). | Add one gesture: swipe-to-dismiss or pull-down sheet using `PanGesture` + `useAnimatedGestureHandler`; combine with Reanimated animated style. | What problem does Gesture Handler solve vs `TouchableOpacity`? When does the gesture run on the JS thread vs UI thread? |
| **17** | RN docs — **FlatList** (`reactnative.dev/docs/flatlist`) + **VirtualizedList** performance guide. | Optimize list screen: add `getItemLayout`, tune `windowSize` + `maxToRenderPerBatch`, memoize row component with `React.memo`, fix `keyExtractor`. Profile before/after with React DevTools or Flipper if available. | What bugs come from a wrong `keyExtractor`? What does `windowSize` control? When does `getItemLayout` give the biggest win? |
| **18** | React docs — **Profiler** (`react.dev/reference/react/Profiler`) + RN performance overview (`reactnative.dev/docs/performance`). | Add `<Profiler>` around the list screen; identify and fix one unnecessary re-render (wrong `useCallback` dep or missing `memo`); document the before/after in a code comment or `docs/perf-notes.md`. | When is `useCallback` NOT needed? When does `React.memo` actually help vs hurt? What is your strategy for measuring before optimizing? |
| **19** | RNTL docs — **Queries + Matchers** (`testing-library.com/docs/react-native-testing-library`). | Add Jest + `@testing-library/react-native`; write 3 tests: (1) pure mapper function, (2) `Button` renders label and calls `onPress`, (3) list renders items from mock data. Prefer `getByRole` / `getByText` over `testID`. | What is the mobile testing pyramid? `getBy` vs `findBy` — when to use each? |
| **20** | RNTL docs — **Async utilities + Providers** (`testing-library.com/docs/react-native-testing-library/api`). | Write 2 integration tests: (1) loading state → success (mock API returns data), (2) loading → error (mock API returns 500); wrap with real Query/Redux provider using test config. | Mock provider vs real provider with test store — which is better and when? How do you avoid tests that depend on execution order? |
| **21** | Maestro docs — **Getting started + Flow YAML** (`mobile.dev/docs`). | Write one Maestro flow: launch app → login with mock credentials → assert list screen visible; add step to run `maestro test` in GitHub Actions (or document the command). | Why few but **critical-path** E2E tests instead of full UI coverage? What breaks E2E tests most often? |
| **22** | OWASP Mobile Top 10 (`owasp.org/www-project-mobile-top-10`) — read M1 (improper credential usage) + M2 (inadequate supply chain security) + M9 (insecure data storage). | Audit the repo: move any hardcoded secret to `.env` + `.env.example`; replace any `AsyncStorage` token with `SecureStore`; add `THREAT_MODEL.md` (5 risks + mitigation per risk). | What is the difference between a threat and a vulnerability? Name 3 things that must never go into logs or crash reports. |
| **23** | GitHub Actions docs — **Workflows + Jobs + Caching** (`docs.github.com/actions/using-workflows`). | Add `.github/workflows/ci.yml`: (1) lint (`yarn lint`), (2) tests (`yarn test --ci`), (3) EAS build dry-run or artifact on push to `main`. Cache `node_modules`. | How does CI help senior teams beyond "it runs tests"? What is the difference between a build artifact and a release? |
| **24** | Sentry RN docs — **Setup + Releases + beforeSend** (`docs.sentry.io/platforms/react-native`). | Integrate Sentry: set `release` + `environment` from EAS env vars; add `beforeSend` to strip PII fields; add one manual breadcrumb for a critical user action; verify error appears in Sentry dashboard (or use demo DSN). | What must NOT go to crash reports? How do you tag releases in Sentry so you can correlate errors to app versions? |
| **25** | EAS Submit docs + App Store / Play Store metadata checklist (`docs.expo.dev/submit`). | Run `eas build --profile preview` locally (or document the steps if no Apple account yet); write `docs/release-checklist.md` covering: version bump, changelog, screenshots, privacy labels, staged rollout steps. | What is a staged rollout? Why use it instead of releasing to 100% immediately? What can you roll back and what can you not? |
| **26** | Apollo Client docs — **Queries + Mutations + Cache** (`apollographql.com/docs/react/data/queries`). | Add a GraphQL endpoint (use a free public API like `countries.trevorblades.com` or a local mock); implement one query + one mutation with Apollo Client; compare cache behavior vs TanStack Query REST approach. | How is Apollo Client cache different from TanStack Query cache? When would you choose GraphQL over REST on a mobile app? |
| **27** | RN Accessibility docs (`reactnative.dev/docs/accessibility`) + WCAG 2.1 contrast checker. | Audit 2 screens with VoiceOver (iOS) or TalkBack (Android): fix missing `accessibilityLabel`, wrong `accessibilityRole`, missing focus order; run a contrast check on theme colors. | `accessibilityLabel` vs `accessible` prop — what does each do? What is the minimum touch target size for WCAG? |
| **28** | — (docs day — review your own `ARCHITECTURE.md` and `THREAT_MODEL.md`). | Finalize `ARCHITECTURE.md` (data flow diagram + auth + error taxonomy + key decisions); finalize `THREAT_MODEL.md` (5 risks, each with: threat, impact, mitigation, residual risk); add `docs/ADR-002` for one more decision made during the 30 days. | Explain the app's security posture to a new team member in 3 sentences. |
